      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There is a great opportunity to make the player UI modifiable through the same great SDK that makes avatars and worlds so great. Being able to carry around an Udon script with you between worlds would do a lot to improve things.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-25T19:32:35.618Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Today, VRC content comes in 2 forms:\n - Worlds, which may take nearly fully advantage of Unity's game development platform\n - Avatars, which are (reasonably) limited to animation and IK scripting for personal expression.\nHowever, as a social VR platform, I'd love to see a third category of content: scripts for the player or client that can change functionality of the platform itself, the same way a web browser addon changes the functionality of the web platform in some way.\nThings like allowing players to customize their client's behavior in worlds (turning off chairs, disabling performance-heavy objects, changing how they move around to support accessibility), plug in to menus to add new options, extend the game with overlays and connections with IoT devices, etc.\nThere was in fact a thriving ecosystem of these until EAC was added, and I think it's really important to the health and future of the platform to have a way to do this. Making it part of the platform rather than something that has to be hacked in or modded would allow VRC to expose a safe API surface that both gives the game the extensibility the community needs to thrive without allowing malicious actors to take advantage of inexperienced users.\nYou can't implement *everything* that the community wants (definitionally: some asks are incompatible, or only viable for a subset of users), and the longer you take to implement the common requests, the less trust there is with the community. Please consider this.",
